        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Ban Chiang culture</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val">Ban Chiang, Nong Han district, Udon Thani province, northeast <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>; related metal finds from nearby Ban Tong, Ban Phak Top and Don Klang; the site of Ban Non Wat is key to its dating.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">Debated: radiocarbon dates put the oldest grave c. 2100 BCE and the first metalworking c. 2000–1700 BCE, while Charles Higham’s Bayesian dating puts first settlement c. 1500 BCE and bronze c. 1000 BCE; the youngest grave dates to about 200 CE.</span></div>
